kosha neon

  -- Ne. proton-10. period 2, group 18 noble gas. valence: 0.
  -- chemically inert — full outer shell, no bonds formed under normal conditions.
  -- second lightest noble gas. glows orange-red in discharge tubes (neon signs).
  -- used as cryogenic refrigerant (liquid Ne at 27K).
  -- formed in stellar nucleosynthesis — abundant in sun and stars.
  -- no stable compounds known under ordinary conditions.

